Name and mark
-------------
This project takes its name and its logo from MicroGridsPy, the micro-grid sizing and
dispatch model developed by the SESAM group at Politecnico di Milano and published under
the European Union Public Licence v1.2:

    https://github.com/SESAM-Polimi/MicroGridsPy-SESAM

It is an independent extension and is not an official MicroGridsPy release, nor endorsed
by its authors. No MicroGridsPy source code is included here; the two projects share no
code beyond the boilerplate every Python file carries.

The two image files below are MicroGridsPy's own and are reproduced unmodified:

    src/microgrid_expansion/ui/static/brand/microgridspy.png
    src/microgrid_expansion/ui/static/brand/logo-square.png


Method
------
The rule-based generation-balance controller this model sizes against follows the policy of
uGrid / uGridNet (Cicilio et al.), which is cited in docs/formulation/references.bib. It was
re-implemented from that published description under this model's own physics rather than
taken from any source: the reference policy updates storage without round-trip losses, has
no minimum stable loading, and lets an uncoverable deficit vanish, and all three would put
the simulated trajectory outside the feasible set the certificate rests on.


